      "response": {
        "text": "Diagnosis:\n- The inode usage on app-3 reached 100%, causing \"No space left on device\" errors, even though disk usage was only 41%.\n- Logs showed that the /var/lib/php/sessions directory had 6.5 million files, exhausting inodes.\n- The tmp-cleaner service, responsible for cleaning up expired session files, had crashed due to a config parse error and was not running.\n\nRemediation:\n- I restarted the tmp-cleaner service.\n- After restart, tmp-cleaner successfully removed 6.1 million expired session files.\n- Inode usage dropped from 100% to 18%, and app error rates returned to normal.\n\nSummary: The issue was caused by tmp-cleaner crashing and not cleaning up session files, leading to inode exhaustion. Restarting tmp-cleaner resolved the problem. No further action is needed at this time.",
